  "id": "Compound::DB00672 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Chlorpropamide, a sulfonylurea compound, is linked to Cyp2c9 through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Chlorpropamide, as part of the sulfonylurea class, binds to Cyp2c9, with Glimepiride and Tolbutamide both being included in the same class and exhibiting similar interactions with the enzyme. This indicates a potential mechanism where sulfonylurea compounds, through their structural properties, influence Cyp2c9 activity. The presence of multiple pathways, including direct binding and indirect effects via porphyria hepatic, highlights the complexity of the relationship. The lowest common ancestors of Chlorpropamide and its metabolites, such as Tolbutamide, point to a shared pathway involving the sulfonylurea antidiabetic agent class, suggesting a broader functional relationship. The integration of these findings supports the idea that Chlorpropamide may modulate Cyp2c9 through sulfonylurea-mediated mechanisms, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
